        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Temperance movement</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> and Ireland, the British colonies including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iceland">Iceland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and France</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">earlier efforts from 1737 and the 1790s; a national movement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> from the 1820s; teetotalism from the 1830s; the Washingtonians from 1840; gospel temperance after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>; a mass movement from the 1860s; national prohibitions in the 1910s and 1920s; decline from the 1930s; still active today</span></div>
